{
  "_comment": [
    "Which NNUEU net each released version was built with. CMake's defaults (FIRST_OUT=32,",
    "head 4/4, DUAL_ACT=0 -> models/w32_wdl0) have never changed, so a plain Release build of a",
    "tag from v0.4.0 on silently produces an engine with the WRONG net. Anything that builds a",
    "git ref must take the widths from here: scripts/nnueu_build_config.py does the lookup and",
    "turns them into -D flags. 'model_dir' is what the built binary must end up embedding (it is",
    "verified after the build) and mirrors NNUEU::DefaultNetDir in src/accumulation.h.",
    "'current' describes the commit that carries this file, so a future tag/branch is",
    "self-describing even before someone adds it to 'versions'. On every release: add the tag",
    "entry AND update 'current'.",
    "Desde v0.4.5 una entrada puede llevar mas flags (f_map, split_ft, ft_phase, third_phase,",
    "psqt_l3, head_sum, head_skip): la red de famG es la primera cuya geometria no se describe",
    "solo con los tres anchos, y construirla sin ellos compila y carga sin protestar produciendo",
    "otra arquitectura. Una clave AUSENTE significa el default de CMake, que es lo que usaron",
    "todas las versiones anteriores, asi que sus entradas no hay que tocarlas."
  ],
